# Wave W17-AA (Route 222): solar turf — beach-road turf, glint flecks: a bright sunlit green carrying pale glint flecks where the light comes off the panels ahead and off the sea beside it, the warmest turf in Borea (design: the panels start glinting a mile before the city does — the turf takes the same light). Route 222’s own ground — split from its twin Route 213’s salt turf by colour entire (sun-green vs salt-olive) and from Lake Gallant’s turf by traffic: this grass is walked to a city, that grass is sat beside a lake.
